Input: {"question": "What is the population of Bennington Township?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 0, "end": 102, "text": "Bennington Township, Michigan Bennington Township is a civil township of Shiawassee County in the U.S."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 103, "end": 121, "text": "state of Michigan."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 122, "end": 179, "text": "As of the 2010 census, the township population was 3,168."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 180, "end": 276, "text": "As of 2010, Michigan's center of population was located in the southeast corner of the township."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 277, "end": 319, "text": "Bennington Township was organized in 1838."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 320, "end": 393, "text": "It was named after Bennington, Vermont the former home of first settlers."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 394, "end": 513, "text": "According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of , of which is land and (0.87%) is water."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d00", "start": 514, "end": 599, "text": "As of the census of 2010, there were 3,168 people, 1,252 households, and 906 families"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d01", "start": 0, "end": 115, "text": "the census [ 1 ] of 2010 , there were 3,168 people , 1,252 households , and 906 families residing in the township ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0417-fd4d249ea05c:d01", "start": 116, "end": 191, "text": "The population density was 82.7 inhabitants per square mile ( 31.9/km 2 